    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1618">

                <pb facs="1319" n="1203" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/129.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram of May 31. The Minister of Public Works is apparently
                    disposed to sign the contract, and the Minister for Foreign Affairs assures me
                    that if signed it will conform to all the conditions of that telegram. He adds,
                    however, that it would seem not proper for the present administration to sign a
                    contract of this nature, as it has only five more weeks of tenure, especially as
                    the President-elect, Porras, recently informed me that he did not approve of
                    constructing this section of the Panamá-David railroad first.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
